1
00:00:00,253 --> 00:00:01,543
(Sheldon:)Would you like to play one?

2
00:00:01,963 --> 00:00:04,093
(Leonard:)- No.
- Oh, come on, it's fun.

3
00:00:04,882 --> 00:00:07,092
Whoo! Another bump.

4
00:00:08,553 --> 00:00:12,053
Okay. Uh, I'll say an element
and, uh, you say an element...

5
00:00:12,223 --> 00:00:15,723
(Sheldon:)...whose name starts
with the last letter of the one I said, okay?

6
00:00:16,894 --> 00:00:17,934
(Sheldon:)I'll start.

7
00:00:19,564 --> 00:00:21,234
"Helium."

8
00:00:24,569 --> 00:00:26,739
Now, you could say, "Mercury."

9
00:00:26,904 --> 00:00:28,444
(Sheldon:)That would give me a Y.

10
00:00:28,614 --> 00:00:31,244
Ooh, very clever. That's a tough one.

11
00:00:31,784 --> 00:00:33,074
So I go with "ytterbium"...

12
00:00:33,244 --> 00:00:34,784
(Sheldon:)...which gets you back to M.

13
00:00:34,954 --> 00:00:36,584
So you go, "Molybdenum."

14
00:00:36,748 --> 00:00:38,748
And I say, "Magnesium."

15
00:00:38,916 --> 00:00:40,206
And you say, "Manganese."

16
00:00:40,376 --> 00:00:42,166
And I say, "Europium."

17
00:00:42,337 --> 00:00:43,967
And you're left with "mendelevium."

18
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:47,090
And there are no more M's,
because I believe that meitnerium...

19
00:00:47,258 --> 00:00:51,178
(Sheldon:)...should still be called eka-iridium.
So congratulations, you win.

20
00:00:55,933 --> 00:00:58,023
(Sheldon:)Do you wanna go again?

